Hello libhdr maintainers,

libhdr 1.2.0 has a heap buffer overflow in `hdr_decode_chunked_value()` in src/hdr.c line 412:
the chunk length is copied with memcpy() without a bounds check.

Steps to reproduce:

```
$ hdrcat --unsafe-fold poc.hdr
==4121==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow on address 0x606000000051
```

Regards
